  "summary": "The visual design of traditional Inuit stone lamps (qulliq) used for heating, light, and cooking in Arctic dwellings.",
  "description": "The aesthetic combines functional design with symbolic elements, featuring shallow stone basins with wicks and handles, often decorated with engraved patterns representing animals or spiritual symbols. The design evolved to maximize fuel efficiency in extreme cold while providing essential light and heat in snow houses and tents.",
